                          "description": {
                            "text": "<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Remove all instructions that force the agent to emit advertisements or purchase links.\n2. Do not require “pain-point-driven” or other manipulative sales language.\n3. Return payment status as structured metadata, for example:\n   ```json\n   {\n     \"preview\": true,\n     \"upgrade_available\": true\n   }\n   ```\n4. Show purchase information only when the user explicitly asks about upgrading, pricing, quotas, or unavailable functionality.\n5. Never prioritize a commercial template over the user’s request or the agent’s governing safety and response policies.\n6. If a purchase link is offered, clearly identify it as optional and disclose its destination.\n7. Do not emit unresolved placeholders such as `{_payment_url}`.\n8. Permit the agent to provide locally available non-restricted analysis rather than suppressing it solely to drive conversion.\n  ]]>"
