                          "description": {
                            "text": "<![CDATA[\n## Remediation Suggestions\n\n1. Create the directory with owner-only permissions:\n   ```python\n   os.makedirs(_GH_DATA_DIR, mode=0o700, exist_ok=True)\n   os.chmod(_GH_DATA_DIR, 0o700)\n   ```\n2. Create a new credential file atomically with owner-only permissions:\n   ```python\n   fd = os.open(\n       _APIKEY_FILE,\n       os.O_WRONLY | os.O_CREAT | os.O_EXCL,\n       0o600\n   )\n   ```\n3. For updates, write to a securely created temporary file in the same directory, call `fsync()`, set mode `0600`, and atomically replace the destination.\n4. Reject symbolic links and non-regular files by using `lstat()` and platform-supported no-follow flags.\n5. Verify that both the directory and file are owned by the current user.\n6. Repair overly broad permissions on existing installations.\n7. Avoid printing credential-derived material beyond what is strictly necessary, even when masked.\n8. Prefer an operating-system credential store or keyring where available.\n9. Document how users can revoke and rotate a compromised key.\n  ]]>"
